  "title": "Canadian and US Fish Found With Rare Contagious Skin Cancer, Scientists Discover",
  "summary": "Scientists have identified a rare and unusual form of skin cancer affecting brown bullhead catfish living in Lake Memphremagog, a freshwater lake shared by the United States and Canada. The discovery is significant because researchers found evidence that the cancer can spread directly from one fish to another, making it the first confirmed case of a transmissible cancer in freshwater fish. The findings, published on July 22 in the journal Nature, provide new insights into how certain cancers ca",
